asus-control-center (1.2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Flatpak distribution, plus the separately packaged host agent
    (asuscraft-agent): a thin, unprivileged, D-Bus-activated session
    service that lets the sandboxed app reach the machine.
  * The host agent holds no privilege of its own: the whitelist-only
    helper and the polkit action io.github.asuscontrolcenter.helper are
    unchanged.
  * Cross-DE support: GNOME 51 and KDE Plasma 6.8.
  * The night light reads and writes the GNOME settings-daemon colour
    schema (enabled, colour temperature, schedule) and keeps the KDE path.
  * The touchpad uses the desktop's own setting; the obsolete xinput path
    is gone.
  * The desktop-environment probe (desktop.cpp) is cached at startup.
  * Fix a double free in the System Diagnosis SMART check (it aborted the
    application on start) and one in the night light's error path.

 -- Mostafa Momen <mostafamomen6521@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:40:00 +0300

asus-control-center (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * System Manager: health overview, CPU/RAM monitoring, Smart Recommendations,
    Quick Actions, health history.
  * Software Center: installed apps, pending updates, driver and diagnostics.
  * Fix memory leak in health-history directory creation.
  * Fix stale helper exit code on spawn failure.
  * Fix health_history.txt file permissions (0600).
  * Fix dead code in autostart scanner (system entries now counted).

